* WHAT IS INCLUDED IN THIS PACKAGE?

<top_level>
    |
    |-- config                    : Analysis configuration XML files
    |
    |-- external                  : External softw. packages
    |      |-- Prob++             : * SuperK's 3-flavour neutrino oscillation package 
    |
    |-- fitter                    : Our main analysis code
    |
    |-- inputs                    : Analysis inputs / data-files
    |      |-- official           
    |            |-- 2010         : Official inputs for 2010 analysis
    |            |    |-- flux    :  from the Beam WG (flux + inputs for norm and shape errors)
    |            |    |-- nd280   :  from the ND280 group (Saclay analysis MC templates for both NEUT/GENIE)
    |            |    |-- niwg    :  from the NIWG (agreed interaction systematics)
    |            |    |-- superk  :  from SuperK (MC templates for both NEUT/GENIE for various selections)
    |            |       
    |            |-- 2011         :
    |
    |-- macros                    : Our analysis procedures
    |
    |-- production                : Batch production scripts for RAL/IN2P3/Oxford farms
    |
    |-- root                      : The `root2k' (ROOT + T2KANA libraries) environment for our analysis macros
    |
    |-- setup                     : Environment setup scripts for various locations


* SETTING-UP YOUR ENVIRONMENT

Use the appropriate script from the setup directory.
The setup script expects a single argument (top-level source code directory).

Example:
% source setup/setup_at_XYZ.sh /path/to/t2kana/nuosc/top/level/dir


* BUILDING THE OSCILLATION ANALYSIS CODE

% cd /path/to/t2kana/nuosc/top/level/dir (or % cd $T2KOSCANA)
% make


* RUNNING THE ANALYSIS MACROS

Use `root2k' instead of `root'.
root2k is root + T2K oscillation analysis library.

